hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16092","He said, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yala ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Jubayr, from Abu Muwayhibah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ordered to pray upon the people of al-Baqi, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon them one night three times. And when the second night came, he said: O Abu Muwayhibah, saddle my mount for me. He said, so he rode, and I walked until he reached them. So he alighted from his mount, and the mount was held, and he stood upon them, or he said, he stood upon them, and said: May what you are in delight you, of what the people are in. Trials have come like pieces of night, some riding upon others, the last severer than the first. So may what you are in delight you. Then he returned and said: O Abu Muwayhibah, I have been given, or he said, given choice of, the keys of what will be opened upon my nation after me, and Paradise, or meeting my Lord. So I said, may my father and mother be for you, O Messenger of Allah, so inform me. He said, that it be returned upon its heel as Allah wills. So I chose meeting my Lord, mighty and majestic. And he did not remain after that but seven or eight until he died (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu al-Nadr said once, returned upon its two heels."
"16093","He said, Yaqub narrated to me, he said, my father narrated to me, he said, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said, Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Abli narrated to me, he said, Ubayd ibn Jubayr, freedman of al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As, narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Abu Muwayhibah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me in the night, and said: O Abu Muwayhibah, I have been ordered to seek forgiveness for the people of al-Baqi, so go with me. So I went with him, and when he stood among them, he said: Peace be upon you, O people of the graves, may what you have come to delight you, of what the people have come to. Had you known what Allah has saved you from. Trials have come like pieces of dark night, the first following the last, the last worse than the first. He said, then he turned to me and said: O Abu Muwayhibah, I have been given the keys of the treasuries of this world, and eternity in it, then Paradise, and I was given choice between that and between meeting my Lord, mighty and majestic, and Paradise. He said, I said, may my father and mother be for you, so take the keys of this world, and eternity in it, then Paradise. He said: No, by Allah, O Abu Muwayhibah, I have chosen meeting my Lord, mighty and majestic, and Paradise. Then he sought forgiveness for the people of al-Baqi, then he turned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began in his pain in which Allah, mighty and majestic, decreed him, when morning came."
"16094","He said, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from Rashid ibn Hubaysh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Ubadah ibn al-Samit visiting him in his illness, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who is the martyr of my nation. So the people fell silent. And Ubadah said, support me. So they supported him. So he said, O Messenger of Allah, the patient, seeking reward. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my nation are few. Killing in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, is martyrdom, and plague is martyrdom, and drowning is martyrdom, and the belly is martyrdom, and the woman in childbed, her child drags her with its cord to Paradise. He said, and Abu al-Awwam, keeper of Bayt al-Maqdis, added in it, and burning, and flood."
"16095","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from a companion of his, from Rashid ibn Hubaysh, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him visiting him in his illness, and he mentioned the hadith."
